{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nrebar's gates verify that a plan is grounded and self-consistent; none asks whether the\nsystem is SIMPLER afterward. The mechanism ratchet\n(`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py`) censuses seven mechanism kinds and blocks an\nunjustified addition, but a `new` key passes on nothing more than a nonblank in-tree\nmarker (`scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py:89-92`), and `parse_marker`\n(`scripts/_mechanism_delta/markers.py:37-44`) yields kind, name and reason. Nothing\nparses a RETIREMENT, and nothing ever revisits a marker once admitted. The ratchet's own\ndocstring records the motive: 56% of sampled fixes added a mechanism against 30% that\nwere pure logic fixes.\n\nPlan review does not close the gap. `A1` is the only complexity criterion and is\nadvisory, at `\"block_threshold\": 0.95` / `\"default_posture\": \"advisory\"`\n(`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json:814-815`).\n\nThis epic makes the gates and the janitor push back on complexity GROWTH, rather than\nonly on complexity that is ungrounded. It was captured 2026-09-07 as an idea from the\ncomplexity-reduction session (session log `59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148`) and authorized at full\nscope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\n\n## Measured facts, re-measured at `origin/main` `b2dca9bf5ea`\n\nThe idea's 2026-09-07 evidence has drifted. Re-measurement, which rescopes two children:\n\n- **The code-review gate is far stronger than the idea recorded.** The idea states only\n  `security` blocks, with `deletion-impact`, `scope-intent` and `tests` advisory. Today\n  **12 of 24** criteria block in `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json`,\n  including `tests` at 0.54 and `deletion-impact` at 0.6. Only `scope-intent` is still\n  advisory. So `f86e` adds a TAXONOMY to an already-blocking `tests` criterion; it does\n  not promote a posture.\n- **Held-out twin modules number 6, not the 88 the idea recorded**:\n  `test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py`, `test_dead_values_heldout_7504.py`,\n  `test_update_priority_heldout_c9c6.py`, `test_code_review_provenance_heldout_2d1c.py`,\n  `test_reviewed_tree_binding_heldout_da31.py`, `test_snapshot_contract_heldout_8537.py`.\n- **\"Seam-guard\" has no referent.** No `*_seam_clean_heldout.py` module exists anywhere\n  in the tracked tree. `d278` is therefore scoped to held-out-twin merging only.\n- **The duplicate-epic evidence holds exactly.** 8 closed epics share the title prefix\n  \"Restore headroom under the 800-LOC module-size cap\", one deliverable filed 8 times.\n- The janitor skill is `examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Why a project overlay, not packaged criteria\n\nThe triggers here are rebar's OWN seven-kind census and its own test conventions, which a\ndownstream consumer does not have; packaged criteria would fire on their plans. The new\ncriteria therefore live in `.rebar/`, the route `project.portability` already takes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\nEach criterion names one deliverable and is delivered by exactly one child.\n\n- [ ] A blocking `project.net-mechanism` plan-review criterion exists in the `.rebar/`\n      overlay, requiring a plan that adds a counted mechanism kind to name the mechanism\n      it retires or state why no retirement is possible. Checked by: `fe94`'s structural\n      tests asserting the criterion resolves, its posture is `blocking`, and its rubric\n      body carries the threshold, finding-fields and non-findings sections.\n- [ ] That criterion is calibrated against a committed eval corpus that demonstrates it\n      fires on real additions. Checked by: `39bc`'s 8-case corpus under `.rebar/evals/`\n      scoring at or above its recorded pass bar, reproducible from the committed spec.\n- [ ] A ticket named as the sunset owner by a `# mechanism-ok:` marker cannot close while\n      that marker is still present in the tree. Checked by: `d68f`'s\n      deterministic completion-gate test closing a fixture ticket with the marker present\n      and asserting refusal.\n- [ ] The code-review `tests` criterion carries a taxonomy distinguishing behaviour tests\n      from tests that pin refactor mechanics, re-export identity, LOC floors, import\n      shape, or re-run a gate script. Checked by: `f86e`'s overlay test asserting the\n      taxonomy text is present in the criterion's rubric.\n- [ ] A deletion-only tidying skill exists separately from the defect audit, whose per-run ticket cap is judged by a non-positive net-complexity budget.\n      Checked by: `6b48`'s assertion that the new SKILL.md admits only deletions and\n      collapses, and names its budget.\n- [ ] rebar-implement's epic-close phase merges held-out twin modules back into their\n      parents. Checked by: `d278`'s test driving the close phase over a fixture epic\n      carrying a held-out twin and asserting the twin is merged.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on `origin/main` with every child landed.\n\n## Child decomposition\n\n- `fe94` crumbly-amphibole-smelts — the net-mechanism criterion. Root; no dependencies.\n- `39bc` lilac-energetic-grosbeak — its 8-case calibration corpus. Depends on `fe94`.\n- `d68f` healthful-childlike-aruanas — mechanism sunset enforcement. Depends on `fe94`.\n- `f86e` unwhite-worrying-bluebottle — the code-review test taxonomy. Independent.\n- `6b48` reservable-honeysweet-chrysalis — the janitor split. Depends on `fe94`.\n- `d278` diseased-head-vervet — held-out twin merging in the close phase. Independent,\n  and narrowed by the seam-guard measurement above.\n\n## Portability and provider neutrality\n\nEvery deliverable is a rubric, an overlay entry, a skill document, or an in-process gate\ncheck. None reads a CI environment, so each behaves identically with no CI provider\nconfigured. The `ci_gate` mechanism kind concerns what a PLAN says it will add, which is\nrecognised from prose. No deliverable names a vendor or needs a model-specific\ncapability, and the new rubrics are `exec: 1-TURN`.\n"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793674928466570001,"uuid":"6da9f1a5-bc7f-4cac-b135-b2a62580b1be"}